@tradition rec-float-hour
// W3 (rec writer; lead 18: fields from plans/rec-traditions-plan.html FINAL and the brief; RA owns the format).
// Float hour: Wednesdays 21:30-22:15 from Day 3, the float room (about 6); Matthias Oduya dims the orbs, quiet music, no
// talking. Tap to float: rest and mood. FOR RA: the float room's places are yours (written as rec:float). Intended who:
// floater (RA's habit) 70%.
k: 492
title: Float hour
when: weekly wednesday from day 3
at: 21:30-22:15
min: 25
where: 7 room Float room: rec:float
who: oduya always, holt 40%, infirmary 15%, everyone 8%
anim: everyone talk
host: oduya
from: oduya
flag: rec.on

== mail
- Float hour tomorrow, {time} in the float room. Matthias dims the orbs, someone plays something quiet, and nobody talks. Come and drift.

== ask
- Float hour tonight. No talking. You'll love it.   #warm
- Coming to float hour? You sleep like a baby after. A tired, floaty baby.   #funny

== here
- Shh.   #warm
- Just drift.   #warm

== thanks
- You step into a fifth of a g as the orbs dim. Nobody says a word. You drift, and the day goes quiet.   #warm

== chatter
- I slept so well after float hour. Best sleep all week.   #warm
- Someone hummed at float hour. Matthias gave them a look. A kind look, but a look.   #funny
- Float hour's the quietest place on the ship.
